
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:nickhash@

%9Parameters:%9

    SHIFT:      Gives the nickname a new color in the channel.

    The channel and the nickname, both exactly as they are displayed; the
    names are case sensitive.

%9Description:%9

    Changes the color that nick hash coloring gives a nickname on a channel
    of the active server. The new color is picked at random from
    nick_hash_colors and differs from the current one. The colors are kept
    in memory only, so they are lost when erssi is restarted.

    The message 'Shifted color' is printed even when the channel or the
    nickname has no color yet, in which case nothing changes.

    Nick hash coloring colors the nicknames in messages (themes can also use
    $nickcolored). Each nickname gets a color from its hash, separately in
    each channel, and keeps it. The related settings are:

        nick_hash_color_enabled (default: ON)
            Enables the coloring.
        nick_hash_colors
            The colors to pick from, separated by spaces: color letters
            such as r, g or B, or #rrggbb values.
        nick_hash_reset_event (default: quit part)
            When to give a nickname a new random color by itself: 'quit'
            (in all channels of the server), 'part' (in that channel) and
            'nickchange' (in all channels, for the old nickname).

%9Examples:%9

    /NICKHASH SHIFT #example alice
    /SET nick_hash_reset_event quit part nickchange

%9See also:%9 FORMAT, SET

